{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"scratchy-leprous-galago","creation_channel":"cli","description":"MCP transition_ticket (and claim_ticket) lack write-param parity with the CLI/lib surface, so agents on MCP cannot perform operations the CLI/lib can. Empirically cataloged by the behavioral-oracle prototype (docs/experiments/write_parity_oracle_prototype.py; evidence on restoring-shallow-blobfish):\n- transition_ticket accepts only (ticket_id, current_status, target_status, close_class); it is MISSING reason, caused_by, ref.\n- claim_ticket is MISSING force.\nConcrete defect (A->C trap): MCP REJECTS a bug-close that requires --reason (reason-required class e.g. not_a_bug) yet has NO reason param to supply it, so a compliant reason-required bug close is UNREACHABLE over MCP. Same for caused_by (culprit attribution) and force (gate bypass).\n\nGovernance basis (operator rulings 2026-08-18): force is allowed through ANY surface; auditability comes from the ABSENCE of a signed attestation (projects gate on certification in CI). So the prior \"intentionally NO force bypass over MCP\" policy is rescinded.\n\nSCOPE: add to MCP transition_ticket: reason, caused_by, ref; add to transition_ticket + claim_ticket: force. Do NOT add force_close (deprecated; removed under a sibling ticket). Update the MCP tool docstrings that assert force is CLI-only.\n\nACCEPTANCE:\n- transition_ticket exposes reason/caused_by/ref/force; claim_ticket exposes force; all delegate to the existing lib core (rebar.transition/rebar.claim) with identical semantics.\n- The behavioral oracle (sibling ticket) cases C/D/E flip from PARAM_NOT_EXPOSED to ACCEPTED on MCP, matching lib; cases A/B stay REJECTED on both.\n- MCP docstrings no longer claim force is unavailable; they state the absent-attestation audit model.\n- make lint + make typecheck green; targeted MCP write tests updated/passing.","id":"1128-505b-54ac-497f","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP transition_ticket/claim_ticket lack reason/caused_by/ref/force parity with CLI/lib"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787080887680395001,"uuid":"dfcf6c5d-db46-45ae-b84c-bacc13d44f57"}